course: dictionary
lesson: 12366
title: Crookedly: not straight
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Crookedly is an adverb. It tells you how something is done or how it is placed. It comes from the adjective crooked, which means bent or not straight. Add -ly and you get crookedly: in a crooked way.
explain: «The picture hung crookedly on the wall.» The picture is not straight, and its frame slants. Try it: if you swap in straight, the sentence changes, so crookedly must describe a way of hanging that is not level.
explain: Crookedly can also describe a smile. «She smiled crookedly at her brother.» The smile is lopsided, pulled up more on one side, and it can show someone is sly or shy. Rarely, crookedly can mean in a dishonest way, but in everyday reading it usually means bent or not level.
fact: Crookedly is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done or placed.
fact: It comes from the adjective crooked, which means bent, twisted or not straight.
fact: «The picture hung crookedly on the wall» means the picture was not level.
fact: «He smiled crookedly» means his smile was lopsided, pulled up on one side.
fact: Rarely, crookedly means in a dishonest way, so always check the other words in the sentence.
exercise: «The picture hung crookedly on the wall.» What does crookedly mean here? | Very brightly | *Not straight or level | Quietly and slowly | Far away from the wall
exercise: «Her hat sat crookedly on her head.» How was her hat sitting? | *At an angle, not straight | Flat and dry | Very tightly, like a helmet | Under the bed
exercise: Miss Ali says the line was drawn crookedly. What does that tell you? | The line was perfectly straight, drawn with a ruler | The line was very long | The line was painted in bright colours | *The line was not straight
test: «He smiled crookedly, as if he had a secret.» What kind of smile is it? | Quick and loud | Cold and angry | *Lopsided and a little sly | Wide and happy, showing all his teeth
test: Which word means the opposite of crookedly? | Quickly | *Straight and level | Loudly | Sadly
exam: Ben's tie was tied crookedly. What is wrong with it? | It is the wrong colour | It is very long | It is made of silk | *It is not straight
